    <h2 style="text-align: center; color: #9C27B0; margin-bottom: 20px;">About Kalathmika</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; color: #444;">
        Kalathmika School of Classical Dance, located in the culturally vibrant town of Aluva, Kerala, is a prestigious institution dedicated to the promotion and preservation of Indian classical dance traditions, particularly Bharatanatyam and Kuchipudi.<br><br>

        Founded with a deep-rooted vision of nurturing artistic excellence.<br><br> Kalathmika provides students with a holistic learning environment where discipline, devotion, and creativity are equally emphasized. The school believes that classical dance is not merely a form of performance, but a path toward inner transformation and cultural understanding.
        <br><br>
        At Kalathmika, students are trained under the guidance of experienced and passionate gurus, who uphold the guru-shishya parampara (traditional teacher-student lineage). The syllabus is thoughtfully designed to cover theory, rhythm (nattuvangam), expressions (abhinaya), stage presence, and performance etiquette.
        <br><br>
        Beyond regular classes, the school actively organizes:
        <ul>
            <li>Annual performances and arangetrams (debut stage performances)</li>
            <li>Workshops by renowned artists</li>
            <li>Participation in national and international cultural festivals</li>
            <li>Community outreach through cultural awareness programs</li>
        </ul>
        <br>
        Kalathmika stands as a cultural sanctuary where tradition meets modern expression, instilling values of respect, grace, and discipline in every learner. The serene campus and the nurturing atmosphere make it a second home for budding dancers who aspire to master the classical arts.
    </p>
